===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|seneschal|lang=enm}} (recorded in English since 1393), from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|seneschal|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|ML.}} (Frankish) {{term|siniscalcus|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|sini-||senior|lang=gem-pro}} + {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|skalk||servant|lang=gem-pro}}; latter term as in {{term|marshal|lang=en}}. Compare French {{term|sénéchal|lang=fr}}.

